{"kind":"request","text":"Security D3, D4, D5 and D6 (6dd06d03 section 6). Agreed direction: these are to be done.\n\nWork:\n1. D3. docs/security/settings.md: every environment variable and binding of each Worker, where it is read, its parser, its failure mode (closed, open or inconsistent), and what /health reports for it. A test enumerates the settings that code reads and fails on a setting without a row.\n2. D4. docs/security/trust-boundaries.md, one section for each deployment: what the session secret, the Artifacts binding, the R2 buckets and the MCP namespaces protect, and which Workers share each one. State finding 3.13: dap-grow and artroom-scope share the artroom-demo Artifacts namespace, the content bucket and the metrics dataset, and only code pins keep them apart.\n3. D5. docs/security/definition-authors.md: what validation refuses and what it allows. List the forms that pass validation and grant more than they appear to: zero guards, approvals 0, an approver action that every role holds, and vacuous guards (count min 0, each over an empty list, ifPresent with the value absent, notIn with no signer, fact with an empty where). Give the fail-open list.\n4. D6. docs/security/threat-model.md: invariants, each with a named witness test, in the style of docs/testing.md. At least: no act takes effect without an observed grant; no outside call without a sealed entry; a session reads only its own membership's scopes; no object exists without a verified genesis; no credential leaves custody except to the key that asked. D1 and D3 are its evidence tables. A script checks that each named test exists.\n5. SECURITY.md at the repository root: points at D1 to D6 and the reviews, and gives a reporting path (GitHub private vulnerability reporting on the dap repository, unless the owner names another). Mark notes/reviews/2026-10-04-security-review.md as a review of the earlier model.\n\nOrder inside: D5 first; D3 after R9 (06-settings) lands; D6 after R2 lands, since its \"no object without a verified genesis\" test needs R2.\n\nWitnesses: the settings test, the named-test check, and a docs link check.\n\nCommon conditions (6dd06d03, review of main 603220b9). Checker review of each exact head before it lands. A head can close part of this request; each head names the findings it closes. The hosted Workers (artroom-scope, dap-grow, dap-lending) stay deployable after each head: the head's report lists every new setting and redeploy step, and the planner deploys after review. No deployment by the builder. Place in the security order: 9 of 10 (6dd06d03 assert lists the order). The archive slices keep priority when one of them is ready to work: F1, 9a, slice 9, F2 (land by 4 November) and F3 (deploy by 6 November).","body":{"conditions":"Four security pages and SECURITY.md, each table held by a test where it can be; closes D3-D6 and documents 3.13. Checker review on every head; hosted Workers stay deployable; no builder deployment.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}